  "verdict_reasoning": "There are 18 bank_transactions rows. All 18 have client_id NULL and bank_account_id NULL. All 18 have org_id set to an org that still exists. The demo seeder (src/demo/seed-ui-coverage.mjs lines 42-48) inserts client_id and subject_client_id FROM THE SAME PARAMETER ($3). So at insert time both held the same value. Today subject_client_id is populated on all 18 rows while client_id is NULL. Two columns written from one value can only diverge if one of them was changed afterwards. client_id carries a foreign key to clients with ON DELETE SET NULL. subject_client_id deliberately carries NO foreign key (db/migrations/101_bank_transaction_subject_anchor.sql). That is exactly the divergence observed. The anchor points at 3 distinct client id(s); 18 row(s) point at a client that no longer exists and 0 row(s) at a client that does. bank_accounts holds 0 rows, and bank_accounts.client_id is ON DELETE CASCADE, so deleting those clients destroyed the account rows; bank_transactions.bank_account_id is ON DELETE SET NULL (db/migrations/092_bank_account_fk.sql) so it emptied rather than deleting the transaction."
